Package: dsFlowerClient
Type: Package
Title: DataSHIELD Client for Flower Federated Learning
Version: 0.4.4
Authors@R: c(
    person("David", "Sarrat González", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "david.sarrat@isglobal.org"),
    person("Juan R", "González", role = "aut", email = "juanr.gonzalez@isglobal.org"))
Author: David Sarrat González [aut, cre],
  Juan R González [aut]
Maintainer: David Sarrat González <david.sarrat@isglobal.org>
Description: Client-side DataSHIELD package for orchestrating Flower federated
    learning under privacy policy enforced by each data node. Builds declarative
    model specifications, verifies the node-installed runner, manages the
    SuperLink and run lifecycle, and supports data-independent public feature
    bounds. Imaging resources are admitted by dsImaging into the DataSHIELD
    session before their opaque handle is passed to dsFlower. Each training
    uses node-owned privacy parameters; arbitrary hook
    code is executed only behind the node's fail-closed sandbox and egress
    policy.
